    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client vs requests.Session: constructor and connection pooling semantics differ slightly; Exception types differ: 
    │   requests.exceptions.HTTPError vs httpx.HTTPStatusError; Timeout semantics differ: requests uses a single float or tuple, httpx uses httpx.Timeout 
    │   object with more granular controls; httpx defaults to not following redirects while requests does by default; If async usage is desired, 
    │   httpx.AsyncClient requires await and async def rewrites, which is a much larger migration
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── requests.Session is used to issue GET requests with a timeout, check status, and parse JSON. httpx offers an httpx.Client with a very similar sync API 
        (get, raise_for_status, json) and can serve as a drop-in for this synchronous usage pattern if httpx.Client (not AsyncClient) is used.

