converted without changing the public API/contract of TelemetryBridge.
    - The 'rc' attribute (via getattr(info, 'rc', 0)) used to build the return dict in publish_reading has no equivalent in amqtt's publish() return value — 
amqtt's publish() typically returns None or an internal message-id object, not an object exposing an 'rc' status code, so the semantics of the returned dict 
cannot be preserved without inventing meaning that doesn't exist in amqtt.
    - client_id and connection parameter handling differ: amqtt expects a client_id at construction time (or auto-generates one) and connect() takes a URI 
string (e.g. 'mqtt://host:port') rather than separate host/port args as in paho's connect(host, port) — this requires restructuring config assembly, not just 
wrapping return values.
    - Even if individual calls are wrapped to bridge sync/async execution (e.g., via asyncio.run per call), this breaks any expectation of a persistent single 
event loop/connection across publish_reading calls in publish_batch, changing behavior and performance characteristics — a structural, not merely syntactic, 
incompatibility.

