  ⚠ Remaining incompatibilities noted by connector LLM:
    - amqtt's entire API (connect, publish, subscribe, disconnect) is coroutine-based and designed to be used inside 'async with' context managers; there is no
synchronous execution path amqtt itself provides.
    - TelemetryBridge.publish_reading and publish_batch are synchronous methods that call self.client.publish(...) and immediately read a return value 
(info.rc); amqtt's publish() is `await`-only and does not return a paho-style MQTTMessageInfo object with .rc/.mid, so the return-value contract cannot be 
preserved even with a wrapper unless the whole call chain becomes async.
    - Making publish_reading/publish_batch async (as required to actually await amqtt calls) would break every synchronous caller of TelemetryBridge — this is 
a propagating structural change, not something a local wrapper around Client() can contain.
    - Connection lifecycle model differs fundamentally: paho uses explicit connect() + background network loop (loop_start/loop_forever) that keeps working 
across multiple independent synchronous calls, whereas amqtt expects connection/session lifetime to be scoped to an async context manager or explicit awaited 
connect()/disconnect() pairs — persistent, freely-reused synchronous connections (as used by _default_client/TelemetryBridge) are not supported without 
restructuring.

