    │   may differ: some libraries use a .compute()/.update() method instead of making the object callable; Attribute names for setpoint/gains may differ (e.g.
    │   Kp/Ki/Kd vs kp/ki/kd); Internal windup/anti-windup and derivative-on-measurement behavior may differ, changing tuning behavior; The comment in this 
    │   file indicates the intended substitution target is actually first-party code, not another PID library — so any library candidate may not match the 
    │   intended migration path
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── simple_pid provides a PID class that is instantiated with gains and setpoint, exposes a mutable .setpoint attribute, and is called like a function to 
        compute the control output. PID-Py and ivPID are alternative third-party PID controller implementations that target the same functional role (discrete 
        PID computation for control loops) and could in principle replace simple_pid's PID class for this same purpose.

