Equivalence Groups Found
└── finite-state machine engine for modeling controller states/transitions
    ├── Candidates : transitions, python-statemachine, pysm
    ├── Used APIs  : Machine, add_transition, model binding (self.state), conditions=, after=
    ├── Pitfalls   : transitions binds transition methods dynamically onto the model object; python-statemachine and pysm require explicit class-based 
    │   state/transition declarations, so call sites like self.start_fill() may need restructuring; wildcard transitions ('*' -> FAULT) are a 
    │   transitions-specific convenience; equivalent must be reimplemented explicitly in other libraries; conditions= and after= keyword semantics differ or 
    │   are named differently across libraries; state attribute access (self.state) semantics and initial-state handling differ between libraries
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── transitions.Machine is used here as a dynamic, model-attached FSM: it binds transition methods (start_fill, level_reached, etc.) directly onto the 
        TankController instance and drives them via conditions/after callbacks. python-statemachine and pysm are the closest functional peers 
        (declarative/programmatic state machines for Python) that could in principle replace this behavior, since they support states, transitions, guards, and
        callbacks. automat was suggested but its API is fundamentally different (decorator-based transition declarations tied to a separate factory/wrapper 
        pattern) and doesn't support dynamically binding a whole transition table via a config dict/list the way this code does, making it a poor practical fit
        here.

