└── email/notification sending
    ├── Candidates : smtplib, apprise
    ├── Used APIs  : SMTP, sendmail
    ├── Pitfalls   : smtplib.sendmail requires a fully-formed RFC822 message string and manual header construction; apprise.notify() takes structured 
    │   title/body arguments instead; apprise abstracts away SMTP entirely behind service URLs (e.g. mailto://), requiring reconfiguration of how 
    │   sender/recipients are specified; Error handling differs: smtplib raises SMTPException subclasses, apprise returns boolean success/failure rather than 
    │   raising; The dependency-injected `smtp` object (with .sendmail) would need to be replaced with an apprise Apprise() instance/notify() call, which is 
    │   not a drop-in swap
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file's own docstring identifies apprise as the intended substitution target for smtplib-based email notifications. Both can deliver a notification 
        message to recipients, but their APIs are fundamentally different (raw SMTP protocol calls vs. a unified notify() call across multiple services).

