    └── All are Python libraries implementing the Modbus protocol for industrial I/O (reading/writing registers over TCP/serial). pymodbus is used here to 
        instantiate a TCP client, connect, and perform read_holding_registers/write_register calls with an isError()/registers response object model. 
        pyModbusTCP, minimalmodbus, and modbus-tk provide equivalent Modbus register read/write functionality but with materially different APIs (e.g., 
        pyModbusTCP's read_holding_registers returns a plain list or None on error rather than a response object with isError(); minimalmodbus is primarily 
        oriented toward serial/RTU communication with methods like read_register/write_register operating on register values directly, not TCP by default; 
        modbus-tk uses a master/hooks-based API). The file's own docstring explicitly flags pymodbus->minimalmodbus as a substitution target requiring glue 
        code, confirming functional equivalence but non-trivial API translation.

