    │   response objects with isError(), while minimalmodbus/modbus-tk typically raise exceptions on failure, requiring changes to the IOError-raising logic; 
    │   umodbus was considered but rejected: it is primarily designed for building Modbus servers, not acting as a TCP master client, so it does not fit this 
    │   file's client usage pattern
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── pymodbus provides a TCP Modbus master client used here to read holding registers and write a single register, with connect() and isError() based error 
        handling. minimalmodbus and modbus-tk both provide Modbus master client functionality (register read/write) that could serve the same functional role 
        of talking to a Modbus device, making them plausible substitutes for the client injected into ModbusIO.

