    ├── Pitfalls   : aiohttp has no synchronous API; all requests must be awaited inside an event loop; Response body/JSON access requires 'await resp.json()' 
    │   instead of direct r.json(); raise_for_status() usage/semantics differ (aiohttp raises via resp.raise_for_status() but only inside async context); Would
    │   require rewriting ScadaClient's public interface (get_demand, get_runtimes, command) to async def, breaking callers
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── aiohttp was suggested as an alternative to requests, but it is fundamentally async-only (async with session.get(...) as resp), whereas ScadaClient 
        methods are synchronous and call session.get/post directly without awaiting. Substituting aiohttp would require converting ScadaClient's methods to 
        async, changing all call sites, and wrapping response handling in async context managers.

