r.json()/r.raise_for_status(), so response handling logic throughout ScadaClient would need to become async as well.
    - Blocking-on-event-loop wrapper tricks (e.g., asyncio.run per call) would not faithfully preserve requests.Session's connection pooling/retry semantics 
and risk event-loop conflicts if ScadaClient is ever used inside an already-running async application — this is an architectural mismatch, not something a thin
wrapper function can correctly resolve.
