    │   synchronous call -- must 'await r.json()'; status_code attribute name is consistent across requests/httpx but aiohttp uses 'status' instead of 
    │   'status_code'
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses requests.Session() to make synchronous GET/POST calls with timeout, raise_for_status(), and .json() parsing. httpx.Client() offers a near
        drop-in sync API (get/post/raise_for_status/json/timeout) making it a genuine substitute, as the docstring itself notes. aiohttp could theoretically 
        fill the same HTTP-client role but is async-only, so using it would require converting ScadaClient's methods to async def and awaiting calls -- a 
        structural rewrite beyond simple import/method substitution.

