    │   entry or a separate awaited coroutine
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── paho-mqtt is used here as a synchronous, callback-based MQTT client to connect and publish messages. aiomqtt, gmqtt, and amqtt are all MQTT client 
        libraries that could serve the same functional role (publishing MQTT messages) and are explicitly called out in the file's own docstring as 
        substitution targets. However, they are async-first libraries (aiomqtt uses async context managers, gmqtt and amqtt are asyncio-based), while the 
        current code uses a synchronous, blocking API pattern (direct instantiation, synchronous connect/publish calls) injected via constructor.

