    - Persisting a live amqtt MQTTClient connection across repeated calls to publish() requires a long-lived event loop; using asyncio.run() per call (a common
sync-to-async wrapper technique) creates/destroys a new event loop each time, which breaks amqtt's internal asyncio-bound state (locks, queues, transport) tied
to the original loop from connect() -- this is a structural async/sync execution-model mismatch, not something a wrapper can transparently paper over while 
